        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Tutorial\n\nLearn Twilite by doing. Each tile is a shelf, and left to right is the order to learn in.\n\n**Start.** Start with your AI, read what a graph is, and set your AI up properly.\n\n**Learn.** The interface, the sixteen primitives (their pages are in the Library), and the how-to guides.\n\n**Go further.** Advanced authoring, and the Glossary for the words.\n\n**Keep what you make.** Saving needs the editor. How billing works is in the how-to guides.\n\nThis graph is a collection. Each tile is a portal it contains, and what a tile shows (its name, its description, how many pieces it has) is read from the graph behind it, so nothing here is a copy."
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1791502752029,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
